# Publish to Scanner

When the codebase changes as part of a requested update, commit that update, push `main` to `https://github.com/JackMiller825/Scanner.git`, and let the GitHub Pages workflow publish it.

- `origin` is `https://github.com/JackMiller825/Scanner.git`.
- This repository and its GitHub Pages site contain only the Token Risk Console.
- Do not commit or push the FOMO marketing site.
- Do not force-push `main`.
- Do not commit `.env`, API keys, wallet credentials, or `data/`.
- Keep the Vite `base` at `/Scanner/` so Pages assets resolve at `https://jackmiller825.github.io/Scanner/`.
- The published root page is the console. GitHub Pages serves the static site only. Live scanner calls stay on `npm run dev` or `npm run preview`.
